From 75f7afe7b1d052b80c570809667e32ee357ecacd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: oneup03 <oneup03@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 05:06:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Build the mod system for mods baked into the executable
 (RECOMP_STATIC_MODS)

For targets that cannot generate or patch code at runtime (the 3DS): mods
are recompiled to C at build time (rt64-3ds tools/mod_bake) and linked in,
each exposing a recomp_static_mod (librecomp/static_mods.h), and every base
function a baked mod replaces or hooks is instrumented by the recompiler
with a check of its dispatch slot at the entry.

With RECOMP_STATIC_MODS the mod system is built as usual (manifests,
config, dependencies, events, section loading, embedded mods), without the
live recompiler, sljit or native code patching:
- StaticCodeHandle stands in for the dynamic-library handle: the same
  pointers, from the baked table, for the mod whose id and mod_binary.bin
  hash it was built from;
- a replacement sets its function's dispatch slot, and hooks are run by
  the slot (recomp_static_dispatch: entry hooks, the replacement or the
  original re-entered once, return hooks), not by regenerating code;
- base exports that take an extra argument go through the baked mod's
  per-import shims instead of generated trampolines;
- the unmet-dependency argument is packed to fit a 32-bit pointer;
- on the 3DS the mods' sections go where the heap would start and the heap
  follows them (the 512 MB model's 0x81000000 is past its 16 MB RDRAM),
  and there are no dynamic libraries.

Only N64Recomp's mod symbol parser is compiled in.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
